#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# laplace_transform

#% text
# `laplace_transform(f, t, s)` gives the Laplace transform `integrate(f*exp(-s*t), [t, 0, inf])` of `f`.

#% text
# `laplace_transform(f, [t1, t2], [s1, s2])` gives the transform in several variables, one after the other.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Sums are transformed term by term; a term with a function that has no definition stays as a `laplace_transform` call.

#% item
# Derivatives of undefined functions give `s^n F(s)` minus the initial values; `integrate(g(u), [u, 0, t])` gives `G(s)/s`.

#% item
# The shift rules: `exp(a t) g(t)` gives `G(s - a)`, `unit_step(t - a) g(t)` gives `exp(-a s)` times the transform of `g(t + a)`; `t^n g(t)` gives `(-1)^n` times the n-th derivative of `G` (when `g` is known; an undefined `g` leaves the call).

#% item
# Bessel functions, error functions, logarithms, integral sines and cosines and Laguerre polynomials come from a table; other integrands go to `integrate`.

#% item
# A value found by a rule or the table is checked against `n_integrate` at a sample point before it is returned.

#% item
# `generate_conditions: true` gives the conditions of convergence of the integral as a `conditional_expression`.

#% item
# A numeric `s` gives the value at that point (the numerical integral when no closed form is found).

#% item
# The result has the precision of `s`: an exact `s` gives an exact value where there is a closed form, a number a machine value, an arbitrary-precision number a value at its precision. There is no `working_precision:` option.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A ramp switched on at `t = 1`:

#% cell
laplace_transform(t*unit_step(t - 1), t, s)
#% output
#= (1 + s)*exp(-s)/s^2

#% text
# The value at a point:

#% cell
laplace_transform(t*unit_step(t - 1), t, 0.3)
#% output
#= 10.700707632069259

#% text
# Two variables:

#% cell
laplace_transform(x*exp(-y), [x, y], [p, q])
#% output
#= 1/(p^2*(1 + q))

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Trigonometric and hyperbolic functions:

#% cell
laplace_transform(sin(w*t), t, s)
#% output
#= w/(s^2 + w^2)

#% cell
laplace_transform(t*cosh(a*t), t, s)
#% output
#= (a^2 + s^2)/((a + s)^2*(a - s)^2)

#% text
# Powers and logarithms:

#% cell
laplace_transform(t^n, t, s)
#% output
#= gamma(1 + n)*s^(-1 - n)

#% cell
laplace_transform(log(t), t, s)
#% output
#= (-euler_gamma - log(s))/s

#% text
# Special functions:

#% cell
laplace_transform(bessel_j(0, a*t), t, s)
#% output
#= (a^2 + s^2)^(-1/2)

#% cell
laplace_transform(sin_integral(t), t, s)
#% output
#= atan(s^-1)/s

#% cell
laplace_transform(laguerre_l(n, t), t, s)
#% output
#= s^(-1 - n)*(-1 + s)^n

#% text
# Derivatives of an undefined function:

#% cell
laplace_transform(f''(t), t, s)
#% output
#= -f'(0) + laplace_transform(f(t), t, s)*s^2 - s*f(0)

#% text
# A delta function and a piecewise function:

#% cell
laplace_transform(dirac_delta(t - 2), t, s)
#% output
#= exp(-2*s)

#% cell
laplace_transform(piecewise([[1, t < 1]], 0), t, s)
#% output
#= (1 - exp(-s))/s

#% text
# A damped oscillation with symbolic parameters; `assumptions:` states what is known about them:

#% cell
laplace_transform(exp(-a*t)*sin(w*t), t, s, assumptions: a > 0)
#% output
#= w/(w^2 + (a + s)^2)

#% text
# Square roots, and an integrand divided by `t`:

#% cell
laplace_transform(1/sqrt(t), t, s)
#% output
#= pi^(1/2)/s^(1/2)

#% cell
laplace_transform(sin(t)/t, t, s)
#% output
#= atan(s^-1)

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# The conditions of convergence:

#% cell
laplace_transform(exp(-a*t), t, s, generate_conditions: true)
#% output
#= conditional_expression((a + s)^-1, re(a + s) > 0)

#% text
# The region of convergence, also for a symbolic power:

#% cell
laplace_transform(t^n, t, s, generate_conditions: true)
#% output
#= conditional_expression(gamma(1 + n)*s^(-1 - n), re(n) > -1 and re(s) > 0)

#% text
# There is no `working_precision:` option; the precision of the result follows the point `s`, here a 30-digit number:

#% cell
laplace_transform(t*exp(-t), t, n(2, 30))
#% output
#= 0.1111111111111111111111111111111111

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The inverse transform gives the function back:

#% cell
inverse_laplace_transform(laplace_transform(t*sin(t), t, s), s, t)
#% output
#= t*sin(t)

#% text
# At a number `s` the value is the integral itself:

#% cell
laplace_transform(t^2*exp(-3*t), t, 2.5)
#% output
#= 0.012021036814425245

#% cell
n_integrate(t^2*exp(-3*t)*exp(-2.5*t), [t, 0, inf])
#% output
#= 0.012021036814425248

#% text
# The point may be complex:

#% cell
laplace_transform(sin(t), t, 1 + 2im)
#% output
#= -1/10 + -im/5

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A transform that the rules, the table and `integrate` cannot find stays a call, although it may exist:

#% cell
laplace_transform(tan(t), t, s)
#% output
#= laplace_transform(tan(t), t, s)

#% cell
laplace_transform(exp(t^3), t, 5.0)
#% output
#= laplace_transform(exp(t^3), t, 5.0)

#% text
# The rules for `t^n g(t)` and for a step times `g(t)` apply when `g` has a known transform; with an undefined `g` the call stays, while the shift `exp(a t) g(t)` is done:

#% cell
laplace_transform(t*f(t), t, s)
#% output
#= laplace_transform(t*f(t), t, s)

#% cell
laplace_transform(exp(-t)*f(t), t, s)
#% output
#= laplace_transform(f(t), t, 1 + s)

#% text
# A number `s` outside the region of convergence stays unevaluated: the integral diverges, and the closed form there is only the analytic continuation, not its value:

#% cell
laplace_transform(exp(t), t, 0.5)
#% output
#= laplace_transform(exp(t), t, 0.5)

#% cell
laplace_transform(exp(t), t, s, generate_conditions: true)
#% output
#= conditional_expression((-1 + s)^-1, re(s) > 1)

#% text
# `working_precision:` is not an option of this function; the call is returned with it:

#% cell
laplace_transform(t*exp(-t), t, s, working_precision: 30)
#% output
#= laplace_transform(t*exp(-t), t, s, working_precision: 30)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `inverse_laplace_transform`, `bilateral_laplace_transform`, `mellin_transform`, `fourier_transform`, `integrate`
